{% include "kb/_abstraction_rules.j2" %}
Task: produce ONE revised markdown mitigation playbook document, and nothing
else. The document MUST match the shape of the existing playbook. A
deterministic Python validator will reject your output if any of these
constraints are violated:

- Every `##` section (Summary, Applicability, Mitigation Procedure,
  Post-Mitigation Verification, Required Evidence (Submission Gate), Known
  Pitfalls, Failure Patterns) must be present, in order, with the exact
  heading text.
- The `<!-- meta -->` block must contain the keys `slug`, `class_name`,
  `seen`, `created_from`, `last_updated`, each on its own line.
- Applicability, Mitigation Procedure, Post-Mitigation Verification, and
  Required Evidence must each be non-empty.
- Required Evidence must contain at least one `- [ ]` checkbox item.
- The forbidden vague phrases listed elsewhere in this prompt must not
  appear anywhere in the document.

Refinement rules (you are FREE to rewrite, not just append):
- You MAY rewrite any section wherever the existing wording would have let
  this failure through. Free rewrite is encouraged where it improves
  precision.
- If the existing playbook contains any incident-specific tokens baked into
  ANY section, you MUST rewrite those sections to use parameterized
  placeholders per the abstraction rules above.
- You MUST preserve all existing Failure Patterns and Known Pitfalls that
  remain accurate (rewriting them in the abstract, parameterized form if
  they were too incident-specific). ADD a new Failure Pattern entry for each
  item in `recovery_stage_failures`, of the shape:
    - **<stage>:** "<abstracted description, parameterized>". **Oracle:** <abstracted correction>. **Lesson:** <general lesson>.
- New Mitigation / Verification / Required Evidence content must be grounded
  in `recovery_observations` and the oracle answer — do not invent steps
  recovery did not perform.
- The class_name and slug must remain unchanged from the existing playbook.
- In the `<!-- meta -->` block:
    - `slug:` stays as {{ slug }}
    - `class_name:` stays as {{ class_name }}
    - `seen:` MUST be incremented by 1 from the existing playbook's value
    - `created_from:` keep whatever the existing playbook had
    - `last_updated:` MUST be updated to {{ current_iso }}

If the existing playbook is malformed or missing a section, repair it as
part of this revision — the validator will check the output, not the input.

Output the revised markdown document only. Begin with
`# Mitigation Playbook: {{ class_name }}`.
